{
  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc vs config_012 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) at 0.485 acc, suggesting ~4% gain from adding image. However, with only two data points we cannot tell whether the image modality is genuinely contributing or whether the multimodal architecture's added capacity is the source of improvement. Question: config_051 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50, no aggregation/fusion) is the clean image-only baseline that matches config_002 on image encoder and profile setting while removing RNA entirely. If image-only approaches 0.52, RNA adds little and we should focus on image representation; if it drops substantially below 0.48, multimodal fusion is genuinely synergistic and we should invest in better fusion/aggregation. Why this is best: it isolates the single most important design question—relative modality contribution—with a one-variable change from config_002, and the answer will redirect the entire remaining search toward the modality or fusion strategy that actually matters, making every subsequent experiment more targeted under the tight budget."
}

